cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PhyloRender in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PhyloRender: a human- and agent-accessible platform for reproducible phylogenetic visualization"
version: "0.8.0"
license: "GPL-3.0-or-later"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jhe1004/PhyloRender"
url: "https://github.com/Jhe1004/PhyloRender"
abstract: >-
  PhyloRender is an open-source phylogenetic visualization platform providing
  both an interactive local web workbench and a Model Context Protocol (MCP)
  server backed by a single deterministic rendering engine. It supports
  phylograms with multi-tree bipartition support matching, fossil-calibrated
  chronograms with official ICS geologic timescales, gene-tree/species-tree
  cloudograms with Java-free 4-category discordance pie charts, and untangled
  tanglegrams, with zero-collision typography, strict collinear multi-tier clade
  brackets, and immutable revision provenance.
keywords:
  - phylogenetics
  - visualization
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - chronogram
  - cloudogram
  - tanglegram
  - reproducible research
